> nthroots 3 8i
the 3 cube roots of 8i (w^3 = 8i)
  w0 = sqrt(3) + i            = 2*e^(i*pi/6)  (principal)
  w1 = -sqrt(3) + i           = 2*e^(i*5pi/6)
  w2 = -2i                    = 2*e^(-i*pi/2)
  check: each w^3, parsed back as printed, equals 8i numerically
> nthroots 4 -16
the 4 fourth roots of -16 (w^4 = -16)
  w0 = sqrt(2) + i*sqrt(2)    = 2*e^(i*pi/4)  (principal)
  w1 = -sqrt(2) + i*sqrt(2)   = 2*e^(i*3pi/4)
  w2 = -sqrt(2) - i*sqrt(2)   = 2*e^(-i*3pi/4)
  w3 = sqrt(2) - i*sqrt(2)    = 2*e^(-i*pi/4)
  check: each w^4, parsed back as printed, equals -16 numerically
> unity 6
the 6 sixth roots of 1 (w^6 = 1)
  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)
  w1 = 1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(i*pi/3)
  w2 = -1/2 + i*sqrt(3)/2     = e^(i*2pi/3)
  w3 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)
  w4 = -1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2     = e^(-i*2pi/3)
  w5 = 1/2 - i*sqrt(3)/2      = e^(-i*pi/3)
  check: each w^6, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically
