> trig atan(x) inverse
  note: x is taken as real
trig forms of atan(x)
  atan via asin: atan(u) = asin(u/sqrt(1 + u^2))
    = asin(x/sqrt(x^2 + 1))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 5e-16)
  atan via acos: atan(u) = sign(u)*acos(1/sqrt(1 + u^2))
    = sign(x)*acos(1/sqrt(x^2 + 1))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 3e-15)
  atan reflection: atan(u) = pi/2 - atan(1/u)
    = pi/2 - atan(1/x)
    for x > 0
    check: equal at 38 of 64 sample points where x > 0 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 26 of 26 points, so the condition is needed)
  atan reflection: atan(u) = -pi/2 - atan(1/u)
    = -pi/2 - atan(1/x)
    for x < 0
    check: equal at 26 of 64 sample points where x < 0 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 38 of 38 points, so the condition is needed)
  atan half-angle: atan(u) = 2atan(u/(1 + sqrt(1 + u^2)))
    = 2atan(x/(sqrt(x^2 + 1) + 1))
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  atan as atan2: atan(u) = atan2(u, 1)
    = atan2(x, 1)
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points
  simplest: atan2(x, 1)  (atan as atan2)
> trig acos(x) inverse
  note: x is taken as real
trig forms of acos(x)
  acos via asin: acos(u) = pi/2 - asin(u)
    = pi/2 - asin(x)
    check: equal at 31 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  acos via asin: acos(u) = asin(sqrt(1 - u^2))
    = asin(sqrt(1 - x^2))
    for 0 <= x <= 1
    check: equal at 18 of 64 sample points where 0 <= x <= 1 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 13 of 13 points, so the condition is needed)
  acos via asin: acos(u) = 2asin(sqrt((1 - u)/2))
    = 2asin(sqrt((1 - x)/2))
    check: equal at 31 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  acos via atan: acos(u) = atan(sqrt(1 - u^2)/u)
    = atan(sqrt(1 - x^2)/x)
    for 0 < x <= 1
    check: equal at 18 of 64 sample points where 0 < x <= 1 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 13 of 13 points, so the condition is needed)
  acos via atan: acos(u) = pi + atan(sqrt(1 - u^2)/u)
    = atan(sqrt(1 - x^2)/x) + pi
    for -1 <= x < 0
    check: equal at 13 of 64 sample points where -1 <= x < 0 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 18 of 18 points, so the condition is needed)
  acos half-angle: acos(u) = 2atan(sqrt((1 - u)/(1 + u)))
    = 2atan(sqrt((1 - x)/(x + 1)))
    for -1 < x <= 1
    check: equal at 31 of 64 sample points where -1 < x <= 1 (max relative difference 2e-16)
  acos as atan2: acos(u) = atan2(sqrt(1 - u^2), u)
    = atan2(sqrt(1 - x^2), x)
    check: equal at 31 of 64 sample points (max relative difference 2e-16)
  simplest: acos(x)  (as given)
> trig atan2(y, x)
  note: y, x are taken as real
trig forms of atan2(y, x)
  atan2 half-angle: atan2(y, x) = 2atan(y/(sqrt(x^2 + y^2) + x))
    = 2atan(y/(sqrt(x^2 + y^2) + x))
    for x > 0 || y != 0
    check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points where x > 0 || y != 0 (max relative difference 6e-16)
  atan2 via atan: atan2(y, x) = atan(y/x)
    = atan(y/x)
    for x > 0
    check: equal at 39 of 64 sample points where x > 0 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 25 of 25 points, so the condition is needed)
  atan2 via atan: atan2(y, x) = atan(y/x) + pi
    = atan(y/x) + pi
    for x < 0 && y >= 0
    check: equal at 15 of 64 sample points where x < 0 && y >= 0 (max relative difference 2e-16)
      (outside: differs at 49 of 49 points, so the condition is needed)
  atan2 via atan: atan2(y, x) = atan(y/x) - pi
    = atan(y/x) - pi
    for x < 0 && y < 0
